// Terrain Effects Chart (printed on the mapsheet), transcribed from
// Manual/Elements/TerrainEffectsChart.jpg.
//
// hexes:    `mp`   movement points to enter a hex of this terrain
//                  (None: land units may not enter);
//           `fire` die-roll modifier to fire at units in the hex
//                  ("-3 to attacker's die roll" = -3; "None" = 0).
// road:     `mp`   movement points to move along a road ("Road: 1"); its
//                  combat effect is "Per other terrain in hex".
// hexsides: `mp`   extra movement points to cross the hexside;
//           `fire` die-roll modifier to fire that enters the target hex
//                  across the hexside;
//           `melee` whether melee may be made across it
//                  (Khor: "May not melee across").
//           City Wall: "+1: may only cross at gate or breech" -- the wall
//           itself is impassable (Wall: mp None), a Gate or Breach costs +1.
//           "-4 to attacker die roll, but see LOS notes" is the Wall's fire
//           effect.
// The Zariba entry is prose only ("Historical scenario only! Considered
// clear terrain in the campaign game.") -- its effects are §9.23.
//
// Printed chart, verbatim (movement point cost / effect on combat):
//   Clear             1                                   None
//   Rough             3                                   None
//   Trees             1                                   None
//   Swamp             3                                   None
//   Nile              Gunboats only 1                     None
//   Hilltop           1                                   None
//   Huts              3                                   -1 to attacker's die roll
//   Building (Named)  3                                   -3 to attacker's die roll
//   Road              1                                   Per other terrain in hex
//   Khor (Stream)     +5                                  May not melee across
//   Crest             +1                                  -1 to attacker's die roll
//   City Wall         +1: may only cross at gate or breech -4 to attacker die roll, but see LOS notes
//   The Zariba        Historical scenario only! Considered clear terrain in the campaign game.
(
    hexes: {
        "Clear": (mp: Some(1), fire: 0),
        "Rough": (mp: Some(3), fire: 0),
        "Trees": (mp: Some(1), fire: 0),
        "Swamp": (mp: Some(3), fire: 0),
        "Nile": (mp: None, fire: 0),
        "Hilltop": (mp: Some(1), fire: 0),
        "Huts": (mp: Some(3), fire: -1),
        "Building": (mp: Some(3), fire: -3),
    },
    road: (mp: 1),
    hexsides: {
        "Khor": (mp: Some(5), fire: 0, melee: false),
        "Crest": (mp: Some(1), fire: -1, melee: true),
        "Wall": (mp: None, fire: -4, melee: false),
        "Gate": (mp: Some(1), fire: 0, melee: true),
        "Breach": (mp: Some(1), fire: 0, melee: true),
    },
)
